ting Deployments, Services, RBAC resources, and monitoring objects. [source: internal/controller/services/auth/auth_controller.go:57-87, internal/controller/services/gateway/gateway_controller.go:41-103]\n395\t- **Gateway ingress chain:** The gateway controller provisions a Gateway API chain: GatewayClass, Gateway, HTTPRoutes, and OpenShift Routes for external TLS-terminated access. A kube-auth-proxy deployment provides OIDC-authenticated access to the dashboard. On OpenShift clusters with integrated OAuth, an OAuthClient resource is created. The controller conditionally creates Istio EnvoyFilter and DestinationRule resources when detected. [source: internal/controller/services/gateway/gateway_controller.go:42-103]\n396\t- **Monitoring data flow:** The monitoring service controller deploys Prometheus proxies (cluster-proxy and namespace-proxy) with kube-rbac-proxy sidecars, a collector for MLflow trace export, and Routes for external Prometheus and Thanos querier access. All monitoring Routes use TLS. [source: internal/controller/services/monitoring/resources/data-science-prometheus-cluster-proxy.tmpl.yaml:59, internal/controller/services/monitoring/resources/data-science-prometheus-route.tmpl.yaml:1]\n397\t- **Security context:** 7 authentication rules and 11 secret references are documented in the Security section. The metrics endpoint enforces Kubernetes authentication and authorization when secure serving is enabled. The operator reads the cluster APIServer TLS security profile to configure its own TLS parameters. [source: cmd/main.go:483-485, pkg/tls/profile.go:151-162]\n398\t\n399\t## Integration Points\n400\t\n401\t- **/v1/ConfigMap:** Controller watch (Owns); protocol: Kubernetes API; purpose: componentHandler. [source: api/common/types.go:4, cmd/component-codegen/go.mod, cmd/main.go:29, 293, 493, 604, 608, cmd/manifest-tools/go.mod]\n402\t- **/v1/ConfigMap:** Controller watch (Owns); protocol: Kubernetes API; purpose: serviceHandler. [source: api/common/typ