{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-fb9e1f07-24cc-482f-97cc-0ab00773cfe6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-acfa1239a775a2af","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-ejx7_xl5/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E001.md","content":"# Structured resource context in manager binary reconciliation error logs\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic converts the rhods-operator manager binary's reconciliation error logs from\nmessage-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs, migrates the\nDSCInitialization (DSCI) controller from non-standard key names to the standard camelCase\nconvention, and adds the `resourceKind` structured field across all controller tiers and\naction files. On completion, every reconciliation error log emitted by the manager binary\ncarries `name` and `namespace` (where the resource is namespaced) and `resourceKind` as\nstructured fields, enabling operators to query logs by resource identity without parsing\nmessage strings.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths across the manager\n  binary to confirm the population of calls embedding resource name or namespace in\n  message strings (the strategy's 75% estimate) and produce a tracked call-site checklist.\n- Convert every audited call site that embeds resource name or namespace in the message\n  string to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`), adjusting message text so\n  resource identity is not duplicated.\n- Migrate the DSCI controller's structured field names from `Request.Name` /\n  `DSCInitialization` to `name` / `namespace` (sites previously identified at\n  `dscinitialization_controller.go` lines 154, 169, 182 and any others found by the audit).\n- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to reconciliation error logs in all controller\n  tiers of the manager binary:\n  - DataScienceCluster (DSC) controller\n  - 8 component controllers (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray,\n    SparkOperator, Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI)\n  - Module controller with its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX,\n    Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator)\n  - DSCI controller\n  - 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup)\n- Apply the same conversion and field additions to all 15 action files across the 4 tiers:\n  - 8 component action files (`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`)\n  - 3 service action files (`services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`)\n  - 1 DSC action file (`datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`)\n  - 3 module action files (`modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`)\n- Handle cluster-scoped resources (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization) so their\n  logs include `name` and `resourceKind` and either omit `namespace` or set it to an empty\n  string — never a spurious value.\n- Author and verify the portion of the CI lint rule / static-analysis check covering the\n  manager binary's converted call sites: the check flags any `log.Error` call in manager\n  scope that embeds name/namespace in message text or omits the required structured\n  fields, and it runs green over the converted codebase.\n- Unit tests asserting field presence and correctness via a test logger for the service\n  controllers, module controller, action files, and cluster-scoped resources.\n- Backwards-compatibility validation per the strategy NFR: before/after log output\n  comparison for a sample reconciliation error; deploy a test build to a dev cluster with\n  the production log consumer stack configured, trigger reconciliation errors, and verify\n  the consumer (Loki et al.) ingests both formats without configuration changes.\n- Coordinate with SRE/Support to identify text-based alert rules that rely on the changed\n  message-string patterns and update them.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a reconciliation error log call in any manager-binary controller or action file\n  that previously embedded resource name or namespace in the message string, when the\n  code is updated, then the call uses structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`)\n  instead — measured by the CI lint rule / static analysis reporting zero remaining\n  `log.Error` calls in manager scope with name/namespace embedded in message text.\n- Given the DSCI controller's reconciliation error logs, when the code is updated, then\n  all structured field names use the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`,\n  `resourceKind`) — measured by a unit test asserting DSCI error logs contain the\n  standard field names and a codebase grep confirming no references to `Request.Name` /\n  `DSCInitialization` as log field names remain.\n- Given a service controller (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup)\n  encounters a reconciliation error, when the error is logged, then the entry includes\n  `resourceKind` — measured by a unit test parsing test logger output and asserting\n  `resourceKind` is present with the correct value.\n- Given an action file error log across any of the 4 tiers (8 component, 3 service, 1\n  DSC, 3 module), when the code is updated, then the entry includes `name`, `namespace`,\n  and `resourceKind` — measured by unit tests asserting all three fields are present with\n  correct values across all 15 action files.\n- Given the module controller or any of its 8 module handlers encounters a\n  reconciliation error, when the error is logged, then the entry includes `name`,\n  `namespace`, and `resourceKind` — measured by unit tests over test logger output.\n- Given the DSC or a component controller encounters a reconciliation error, when the\n  error is logged, then the entry includes `resourceKind` — measured by unit tests over\n  test logger output (bundled P1 requirement: added in the same pass as the P