{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf1645d94dd26395","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n3\ttitle: Structured resource context in manager binary reconciliation error logs\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: null\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Structured resource context in manager binary reconciliation error logs\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic converts the rhods-operator manager binary's reconciliation error logs from\n34\tmessage-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs, migrates the\n35\tDSCInitialization (DSCI) controller from non-standard key names to the standard camelCase\n36\tconvention, and adds the `resourceKind` structured field across all controller tiers and\n37\taction files. On completion, every reconciliation error log emitted by the manager binary\n38\tcarries `name` and `namespace` (where the resource is namespaced) and `resourceKind` as\n39\tstructured fields, enabling operators to query logs by resource identity without parsing\n40\tmessage strings.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths across the manager\n45\t  binary to confirm the population of calls embedding resource name or namespace in\n46\t  message strings (the strategy's 75% estimate) and produce a tracked call-site checklist.\n47\t- Convert every audited call site that embeds resource name or namespace in the message\n48\t  string to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`), adjusting message text so\n49\t  resource identity is not duplicated.\n50\t- Migrate the DSCI controller's structured field names from `Request.Name` /\n51\t  `DSCInitialization` to `name` / `namespace` (sites previously identified at\n52\t  `dscinitialization_controller.go` lines 154, 169, 182 and any others found by the audit).\n53\t- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to reconciliation error logs in all controller\n54\t  tiers of the manager binary:\n55\t  - DataScienceCluster (DSC) controller\n56\t  - 8 component controllers (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray,\n57\t    SparkOperator, Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI)\n58\t  - Module controller with its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX,\n59\t    Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator)\n60\t  - DSCI controller\n61\t  - 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup)\n62\t- Apply the same conversion and field additions to all 15 action files across the 4 tiers:\n63\t  - 8 component action files (`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`)\n64\t  - 3 service action files (`services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`)\n65\t  - 1 DSC action file (`datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`)\n66\t  - 3 module action files (`modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`)\n67\t- Handle cluster-scoped resources (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization) so their\n68\t  logs include `name` and `resourceKind` and either omit `namespace` or set it to an empty\n69\t  string — never a spurious value.\n70\t- Author and verify the portion of the CI lint rule / static-analysis check covering the\n71\t  manager binary's converted call sites: the check flags any `log.Error` call in manager\n72\t  scope that embeds name/namespace in message text or omits the required structured\n73\t  fields, and it runs green over the converted codebase.\n74\t- Unit tests asserting field presence and correctness via a test logger for the service\n75\t  controllers, module controller, action files, and cluster-scoped resources.\n76\t- Backwards-compatibility validation per the strategy NFR: before/after log output\n77\t  comparison for a sample reconciliation error; deploy a test build to a dev cluster with\n78\t  the production log consumer stack configured, trigger reconciliation errors, and verify\n79\t  the consumer (Loki et al.) ingests both formats without configuration changes.\n80\t- Coordinate with SRE/Support to identify text-based alert rules that rely on the changed\n81\t  message-string patterns and update them.\n82\t\n83\t## Acceptance Criteria\n84\t\n85\t- Given a reconciliation error log call in any manager-binary controller or action file\n86\t  that previously embedded resource name or namespace in the message string, when the\n87\t  code is updated, then the call uses structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`)\n88\t  instead — measured by the CI lint rule / static analysis reporting zero remaining\n89\t  `log.Error` calls in manager scope with name/namespace embedded in message text.\n90\t- Given the DSCI controller's reconciliation error logs, when the code is updated, then\n91\t  all structured field names use the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`,\n92\t  `resourceKind`) — measured by a unit test asserting DSCI error logs contain the\n93\t  standard field names and a codebase grep confirming no references to `Request.Name` /\n94\t  `DSCInitialization` as log field names remain.\n95\t- Given a service controller (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup)\n96\t  encounters a reconciliation error, when the error is logged, then the entry includes\n97\t  `resourceKind` — measured by a unit test parsing test logger output and asserting\n98\t  `resourceKind` is present with the correct value.\n99\t- Given an action file error log across any of the 4 tiers (8 component, 3 service, 1\n100\t  DSC, 3 module), when the code is updated, then the entry includes `name`, `namespace`,\n101\t  and `resourceKind` — measured by unit tests asserting all three fields are present with\n102\t  correct values across all 15 action files.\n103\t- Given the module controller or any of its 8 module handlers encounters a\n104\t  reconciliation error, when the error is logged, then the entry includes `name`,\n105\t  `namespace`, and `resourceKind` — measured by unit tests over test logger output.\n106\t- Given the DSC or a component controller encounters a reconciliation error, when the\n107\t  error is logged, then the entry includes `resourceKind` — measured by unit tests over\n108\t  test logger output (bundled P1 requirement: added in the same pass as the P0\n109\t  conversion at the same call sites).\n110\t- Given a cluster-scoped resource (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization) is\n111\t  reconciled and encounters an error, when the error is logged, then the entry includes\n112\t  `name` and `resourceKind` and `namespace` is omitted or empty — measured by a unit\n113\t  test confirming cluster-scoped resources do not emit a spurious namespace value.\n114\t- Given the manager binary's converted call sites, the CI lint rule / static-analysis\n115\t  check covering those sites is authored, wired into CI, and passes over the converted\n116\t  codebase while demonstrably flagging a non-conforming call in a fixture.\n117\t- Given the log format change, before/after log output for a sample reconciliation error\n118\t  shows structured fields present, the production log consumer stack on a dev cluster\n119\t  ingests both formats without configuration changes, and text-based alert rules relying\n120\t  on changed message patterns are identified with SRE/Support and updated — measured by\n121\t  the before/after comparison record and the dev-cluster ingestion verification.\n122\t\n123\t## HLR Traceability\n124\t\n125\t- HLR-1 (P0) — manager-binary portion: conversion of message-embedded name/namespace to\n126\t  structured KV pairs across all controller tiers and action files in the manager binary.\n127\t- HLR-2 (P0) — DSCI controller migration to standard key names.\n128\t- HLR-3 (P0) — `resourceKind` in service controller reconciliation error logs.\n129\t- HLR-4 (P0) — `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` in all 15 action files across 4 tiers.\n130\t- HLR-6 (P0) — `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` in module controller error logs\n131\t  (8 module handlers).\n132\t- HLR-7 (P1, bundled) — `resourceKind` in DSC and component controller error logs; not\n133\t  separately schedulable because it is added at the exact call sites rewritten for the\n134\t  P0 conversion in the same files, and a split would audit the same files twice.\n135\t\n136\t## Notes\n137\t\n138\t- Effort context: the strategy prices the audit (~0.5 sprint) and conversion (~0.75–1\n139\t  sprint) for this scope; the epic is kept whole as one mechanical pass and carries a\n140\t  documented re-split trigger in the decomposition summary (split along the\n141\t  controller-tier vs action-file boundary if the audit shows a materially higher\n142\t  call-site count than the 75% estimate).\n143\t- The audit that confirms the actual percentage of embedded-identity calls is the first\n144\t  phase of this epic's work; it does not gate any other epic.\n145\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-baca80cab9da882e","agent_id":"a9df7a535a36364ba","session_id":"c08e1838-c4fd-42e6-9ea2-693cdf6b9521","uuid":"54c4e1b0-2ca9-44f9-a4f8-937fffa7cd91","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:54:11.744Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf1645d94dd26395","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
