{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-91c2cd5266e3a912","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E003\n3\ttitle: 'Structured log field convention: contribution guideline and external publication'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n13\tai_signals:\n14\t  change_specificity: 1\n15\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n16\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n17\t  existing_foundation: 1\n18\t  open_questions: 0\n19\t  external_dependency: 0\n20\t  human_process_gates: -1\n21\t  repo_access: 1\n22\t  architecture_claims: 1\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 3\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Structured log field convention: contribution guideline and external publication\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tThis epic documents the structured reconciliation-log field convention as a contribution\n36\tguideline for new controller development in the rhods-operator codebase and publishes the\n37\tconvention as a specification for external operator teams (Cluster Observability Operator:\n38\tLoki Operator, Tempo Operator) for voluntary adoption per platform policy (overlay 0008 —\n39\tRHOAI does not install, manage, or control external operator dependencies). The guideline\n40\tcaptures the three-problem diagnosis, the required field set, and the migration guidance\n41\tfor the DSCI key-name change.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\tContent outline:\n46\t\n47\t- **Contribution guideline (rhods-operator repo)** specifying:\n48\t  - Required structured fields for reconciliation error logs: `name`, `namespace`\n49\t    (omitted or empty for cluster-scoped resources), and `resourceKind`.\n50\t  - camelCase naming rationale — alignment with controller-runtime's existing structured\n51\t    log key conventions.\n52\t  - The three-problem diagnosis: message-embedded resource identity, DSCI non-standard\n53\t    key names (`Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization`), and missing `resourceKind`.\n54\t  - Before/after code examples for converting message-embedded identity to structured\n55\t    key-value pairs (e.g., `log.Error(err, \"failed to reconcile Dashboard 'example' in\n56\t    namespace 'redhat-ods-applications'\")` becoming `log.Error(err, \"reconciliation\n57\t    failed\", \"name\", \"example\", \"namespace\", \"redhat-ods-applications\", \"resourceKind\",\n58\t    \"Dashboard\")`).\n59\t  - Cluster-scoped resource handling (no spurious `namespace` value).\n60\t  - How the CI lint rule / static-analysis check enforces the convention for new code.\n61\t- **DSCI key migration guide** for operators: release-notes-ready documentation of the\n62\t  `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` → `name`/`namespace` migration with before/after\n63\t  Loki/CloudWatch query examples, supporting a single-release transition.\n64\t- **Published convention specification for external operators**: the field convention,\n65\t  rationale, and adoption guidance, published where the COO team (Loki Operator, Tempo\n66\t  Operator) can consume it; file tracking issues in the COO projects per the strategy's\n67\t  risk mitigation, acknowledging adoption is best-effort and at their discretion.\n68\t- Design-doc reconciliation: fold the strategy's \"to be created\" design doc intent\n69\t  (three-problem diagnosis, before/after examples, DSCI migration guide) into this\n70\t  guideline rather than producing a separate overlapping document.\n71\t\n72\t## Acceptance Criteria\n73\t\n74\t- The contribution guideline exists in the rhods-operator repository and specifies the\n75\t  required fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`), the camelCase naming rationale,\n76\t  and the three-problem diagnosis — measured by review of the published guideline\n77\t  against this checklist.\n78\t- The guideline includes before/after code examples for converting message-embedded\n79\t  identity and documents cluster-scoped resource handling — measured by the examples\n80\t  being present and consistent with the implemented logging behavior.\n81\t- The DSCI key-name migration is documented with before/after log-query examples\n82\t  suitable for release notes — measured by the migration section covering both the old\n83\t  and new field names.\n84\t- The convention is published as a specification accessible to the external operator\n85\t  teams, and tracking issues are filed in the COO projects — measured by the publication\n86\t  location and the filed issues.\n87\t- The guideline is technically reviewed against the implemented logging changes in both\n88\t  operator binaries (manager and cloudmanager) — measured by a recorded technical review\n89\t  confirming the documented convention matches the shipped log output, including field\n90\t  names and cluster-scoped behavior.\n91\t\n92\t## HLR Traceability\n93\t\n94\t- HLR-8 (P1) — document the convention as a contribution guideline for new controller\n95\t  development and publish it for external operator adoption.\n96\t\n97\t## Notes\n98\t\n99\t- Depends on the implementation of the structured logging conversion in both operator\n100\t  binaries being final: the guideline documents what was actually built, including the\n101\t  DSCI migration and cluster-scoped resource behavior.\n102\t- Open question (PM / Observability team): whether the convention should include fields\n103\t  beyond name/namespace/kind (e.g., reconciliation attempt count, error category). The\n104\t  required field set is fixed by this strategy; any extension is an additive PM decision\n105\t  that can be layered onto the guideline later and does not gate this epic.\n106\t- External adoption by the COO team is voluntary and outside this strategy's control;\n107\t  the deliverable here is the published convention and the filed tracking issues, not\n108\t  adoption itself.\n109\t- Documentation Support is listed as \"_Pending human review_\" in the strategy's\n110\t  prerequisites; this epic should be routed through that gate when scheduled.\n111\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-baca80cab9da882e","agent_id":"a9df7a535a36364ba","session_id":"c08e1838-c4fd-42e6-9ea2-693cdf6b9521","uuid":"e0b2257b-cc22-49a4-afa8-2593f3b134a1","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:54:13.281Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-91c2cd5266e3a912","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
